Hi there, 

Maddie here from Originality.AI!

This past week has been a wild one in the AI world with all of the Sam
Altman and OpenAI Drama. With the situation changing daily, it was a bit
hard to keep up with, which gave us a fun and unique opportunity to test
out ourFact-Checking tool  in
real-time! 

We asked chatGPT some questions about the ongoing situation, which it
could not answer- and was pretty honest about its own limitations.

In contrast, we took some content from an article

that summarized the situation quite well and scanned it through
Originality.AI's Fact- Checking tool. It was able to detect the true
fact ( that OpenAI's CEO had been fired on November 17th) but also,
was able to name Sam Altman in the explanation, even though the in text
fact did not mention him by name. 

Our Fact-Checking tool was also able to correctly identify some facts
about Microsoft hiring Sam Altman and his co-founder Greg Brockman after
the ousting.  

Check out our Fact-Checking Tool 

What truly sets our Fact-Checking tool apart is our real-time
capabilities. In the fast-paced world we live in, information evolves
rapidly, and the ability to stay informed with ongoing situations is
important! Unlike some other AI models, Originality.AI's Fact-Checking
tool has the ability to keep up with real-time information ( or drama
) , ensuring you have the most current and accurate information and
resources available to you. 

****Featured Originality.AI Study****

G2 reviews Case Study-  187,000 reviews, 15,231 companies. The
Originality.ai AI detector distinguishes between human and AI-generated
content in B2B software reviews.

